= Five-order missing-price result
The frozen native analyzer rederived 60 matched threshold rows from
independently replayed complete-solve records. At 64 public targets,
median extra omitted rho group-addition equivalents per observed step
needed to tie the full-image *group-count lower bound* were 112.973,
303.573, 334.844, 288.595 and 1,390.865 at orders 229, 421, 433,
457 and 1,201. The order-1,201 three-round minimum and maximum were
1,266.482 and 1,575.602. All historical 48 rows were unchanged.

#image("GRAPH.svg", width: 100%)

This threshold assumes every omitted full-image operation costs zero;
it is neither an observed rho primitive price nor a complete portable
addition-equivalent `S`. The complete-price protocol still requires
disjoint counts and host-class calibration. Exact inputs, commands,
output hashes and the 60-row JSON are linked from `REPORT.md` and
`sensitivity_five/RESULTS.md`. The five field primes and cofactors vary;
no exponent or end-to-end speed ratio is inferred.
